lved in IgE receptor-mediated mast cell degranulation. <source>Int. Immunol.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>573</fpage>&#x02013;580.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10744659</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Gonzalez-Espinosa, C., S. Odom, A. Olivera, J.P. Hobson, M.E. Martinez, A. Oliveira-Dos-Santos, L. Barra, S. Spiegel, J.M. Penninger, and J. Rivera. <year>2003</year>. Preferential signaling and induction of allergy-promoting lymphokines upon weak stimulation of the high affinity IgE receptor on mast cells. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>197</volume>:<fpage>1453</fpage>&#x02013;1465.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12782712</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Goode, B.L., D.G. Drubin, and G. Barnes. <year>2000</year>. Functional cooperation between the microtubule and actin cytoskeletons. <source>Curr. Opin. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>63</fpage>&#x02013;71.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10679357</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Gu, H., and B.G. Neel. <year>2003</year>. The &#x0201c;Gab&#x0201d; in signal transduction. <source>Trends Cell Biol.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>122</fpage>&#x02013;130.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12628344</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Gu, H., K. Saito, L.D. Klaman, J. Shen, T. Fleming, Y. Wang, J.C. Pratt, G. Lin, B. Lim, J.P. Kinet, and B.G. Neel. <year>2001</year>. Essential role for Gab2 in the allergic response. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>412</volume>:<fpage>186</fpage>&#x02013;190.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11449275</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Guo, Z., C. Turner, and D. Castle. <year>1998</year>. Relocation of the t-SNARE SNAP-23 from lamellipodia-like cell surface projections regulates compound exocytosis in mast cells. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>94</volume>:<fpage>537</fpage>&#x02013;548